TEXT 0 -352 Left 2 ;Second-order all-pass with an op amp: R1 and the series L1-C1 are a notch into the + input, and R2 = R3 make the amplifier subtract the input (U1 has no poles: only its gain):\nout = 2·V(+) − in, that is, H(s) = V(out) / V(in) = (s² − s ω0/Q + ω0²) / (s² + s ω0/Q + ω0²) with ω0 = 1/√(LC) and Q = √(L/C) / R1 ≈ 2.1.\n|H| = 1 at every frequency and the phase goes from 0 to −360° (−180° at f0 ≈ 5.03 kHz). The zeros are the poles mirrored on the right half-plane.\nStep: out jumps to 1 (at first L1 is an open circuit), dips to about 0.3, rings and settles back at 1.
